inferno: race-free flow teardown on link loss

On link loss the RX flow times out (~2s no media) and teardown races
with the channel (dis)connect and update paths: flows_info[i] and the
UnicastFlow handle can already be cleared when they are unwrapped -
the panic poisons the flows_info lock and cascades through every
task touching it (info_mcast_server, channels_subscriber). The inferno
runtime is left half-torn-down: the PCM reader keeps wrapping stale
ring content (the sink loops the last buffer) and the subscriber is
dead (no subscription resume after the link returns).

Guard the race instead of unwrapping: connect/disconnect_channel skip
when the flow entry is gone, the tx-channel update path skips flows
without a handle, and the removal path still removes the socket when
the handle is already cleared (it only skips the stop_flow request;
keepalive loss kicks the tx side off anyway).

Signed-off-by: virgilio firmware
